meta {
  name: Full reset
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/admin/reset
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Run this before every session. Ordering matters and is why this exists as one
  operation rather than three:

    1. close open ISBM sessions - must happen while the ids are still readable,
       or they leak on the provider
    2. delete and recreate channels - discards publications posted before the
       reset, which the next run would otherwise read as its own
    3. drop and recreate the SQL tables

  Failures at steps 1 and 2 are logged and do not abort: a session or channel the
  provider has already forgotten is the desired end state.

  After this, run "ENG - add tag" onwards. Channels are already created, so
  "ISBM - ensure channels" is not needed.
}
